<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Columba livia Turing wavelength at 256 um (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring names each equation's source. sigma_plus is the Turing growth rate, analytical_kc2 is the critical-wavenumber formula, and the Lean declarations are listed in the math-KG YAML with line loci. The time-scale factor S is documented as a clock, not a biological rate." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Columba livia Turing wavelength at 256 um (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the Schnakenberg linearization (sigma_plus), the critical-wavenumber formula that pins lambda_c at 256 um, and an IMEX Fourier step. Four Lean theorems with zero sorry cover the determinant sign, the equal-diffusion ablation, the four-wavelength domain, and the Holocene 1/1 scale succession. Parameters are reconstructed for this scale rather than copied from a pigeon-specific published table, which is why the score is not higher." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Columba livia Turing wavelength at 256 um (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) — Morphometric validation: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "measure_morphoeval reports Pearson r = 0.999889 against the analytic dispersion (reference 1; unscaled RMSE 0.0511), stripe spacing CV, an ablation ratio of 0.0177 against a reference of 0, specimen foreground fraction 0.5577 against a balanced-frame null of 0.5, contour circularity 0.0145 against a circle null of 1, and a luminance KS of 0.387 against identical-distribution 0. The saturated stripe mode is n = 4, so the realized wavelength is 256 um on the 1024 um domain." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
