    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Columba livia Turing wavelength at 256 um (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) (Columba livia)",
        "Columba livia Turing wavelength at 256 um (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) faithfully reproduces Columba livia morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Columba livia specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Columba livia" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A fossil transition, a change in age, or a calibrated micrometre measurement off the photograph (the file has no scale bar).",
        "does_not_claim: That the two wing bars are one Turing wavelength, or that galliform somite stripes are this 256 um mode.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 1 GIF is the bare melanin field (--render-mode unfitted). Computer-vision similarity to the flight photograph was 57.8.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Stripe anisotropy (Dv_y/Du=2.5, below threshold) versus isotropic spots is a reconstructed switch at fixed k_c, not a measured NDP-to-diffusion map.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=0.90, Dv/Du=10, gamma0=pi^2/22.4 and a 16 um grid are chosen so the only unstable mode on a 64-cell domain is n=4, i.e. lambda_c=256 um. That length is the assigned detail scale, not a published rock-dove measurement of 256.000 um.",
        "reported_in_source: Prum & Williamson (2002) treat within-feather bars, spots and ocelli as reaction-diffusion patterns.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the two-species kinetics. Murray (1981) shows the same mechanism can make stripes or spots.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a wavelength where the dispersion relation has a positive growth rate.",
        "reported_in_source: Vickrey et al. (2018) map rock-dove checker versus bar to NDP alleles. Haupaix et al. (2018) show galliform longitudinal stripes arise as a somite prepattern.",
        "transfer_boundary: Periodic 1024 um vane patch at age 0 Ma. The chronoseries has one entry, so there is no other Columba chronospecies to difference. The predecessor scale is the 24.1 um diffusion length; the successor scale is a 2560 um packet, still below the centimetre wing bar." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Columba livia" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Columba" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/columba_livia_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Columba livia; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a wavelength where the dispersion relation has a positive growth rate. | Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the two-species kinetics. Murray (1981) shows the same mechanism can make stripes or spots. | Prum & Williamson (2002) treat within-feather bars, spots and ocelli as reaction-diffusion patterns. | Vickrey et al. (2018) map rock-dove checker versus bar to NDP alleles. Haupaix et al. (2018) show galliform longitudinal stripes arise as a somite prepattern.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=0.90, Dv/Du=10, gamma0=pi^2/22.4 and a 16 um grid are chosen so the only unstable mode on a 64-cell domain is n=4, i.e. lambda_c=256 um. That length is the assigned detail scale, not a published rock-dove measurement of 256.000 um. | Stripe anisotropy (Dv_y/Du=2.5, below threshold) versus isotropic spots is a reconstructed switch at fixed k_c, not a measured NDP-to-diffusion map. | Pass 1 GIF is the bare melanin field (--render-mode unfitted). Computer-vision similarity to the flight photograph was 57.8.; transfer_boundary: Periodic 1024 um vane patch at age 0 Ma. The chronoseries has one entry, so there is no other Columba chronospecies to difference. The predecessor scale is the 24.1 um diffusion length; the successor scale is a 2560 um packet, still below the centimetre wing bar.; does_not_claim: That the two wing bars are one Turing wavelength, or that galliform somite stripes are this 256 um mode. | A fossil transition, a change in age, or a calibrated micrometre measurement off the photograph (the file has no scale bar).]; phenomenon_size: 220 µm (0.0002202 m, log10=-3.657 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 220 µm to 65.7 cm): 220 µm:columba-livia-bioelectric-polarity, 800 µm:columba-livia-vertex-packing, 1.5 cm:columba-livia-turing-wavelength, 2.7 cm:columba-livia-clock-wavefront, 4.5 cm:columba-livia-morphogen-condensation, 5.8 cm:columba-livia-flux-canalization, 6.5 cm:columba-livia-elastic-buckling, 14.3 cm:columba-livia-branching-tree" ;
